BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260425T160000Z
DTEND:20260425T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260425T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Librarians - Indie Lens Pop-Up Screening with PBS NC
DESCRIPTION:Eventbrite registration link\n\nIn Partnership with PBS North 
 Carolina we invite you to:\n\n\n\nIndie Lens Pop-Up Screening: The 
 Librarians\nSaturday\, April 25 | 12:00 PM – 2 PM\nDurham County Main 
 Library\n300 N Roxboro Street\, Durham\n\nEventbrite registration 
 link\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Librarians examines the growing national movement to 
 challenge library collections\, particularly books addressing race\, 
 history\, and LGBTQIA  identities. Through firsthand accounts and 
 historical context\, the film explores what these efforts mean for 
 libraries\, education and democracy.\n\n\n\nFollowing the screening\, 
 we’ll host a community conversation and Q&A with librarians and educators 
 focused on intellectual freedom\, access to information\, and the role of 
 libraries as civic institutions.\n\n\n\nEventbrite registration 
 link\n\nWatch The Librarians Trailer\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWhere can I 
 park when the Main Library parking lot is full?\n\nParking is available in 
 the library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 
 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly across the 
 street from the library. Parking is free in the garage. Please bring your 
 ticket to a service desk in the library for validation.\n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham Library Foundation, Humanities, Library Fest, Movie
UID:LibCal-14288-16605205
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16605205
END:VEVENT
