BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260429T220000Z
DTEND:20260429T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260429T000000Z
SUMMARY:Comets\, Clues\, and Our Cosmic Story (Citizen Science Month)
DESCRIPTION:Comets\, Clues\, and Our Comic Story\n\nApril 29\, 2026 at 6pm 
 ET\n\nLearn about the origins of our solar system as you scan online images 
 from space.\n\nJoin us in-person to view online images from a NASA 
 observatory and learn how to identify and report comets and other space 
 objects. Each comet you discover offers clues about how planetary systems 
 form and the possible origins of Earth’s water. The NASA-supported 
 project leader will join us via Zoom to describe the research and answer 
 any questions we have as we participate in “Rubin Comet Catchers” 
 together.\n\nJoin us and be part of 2.50 Million Acts of Science this April 
 during Citizen Science Month. No experience needed—just curiosity!  
 \n\nPlease bring a device (phone\, laptop\, or tablet) if you can. Limited 
 devices are available.
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaris T.":MAILTO:amaristorres@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Community Engagement, Digital/Tech Literacy, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16418146
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/calendar/14288/cometcatchers
END:VEVENT
