SUMMARY:Drop-In Tech Support
DESCRIPTION:\n\nHave questions about your computer\, laptop\, or tablet? 
 Drop in for friendly\, hands-on tech support. Get help with any general 
 technology issue. No question is too 
 basic!\n\nWhen\n\n\n	Tuesdays\n	6:00–7:00 PM\n	Drop in anytime during the 
 hour.\n\n\nWhat You Can Get Help With\n\n\n	Getting started with 
 computers\, laptops\, or tablets\n	Setting up email accounts\n	Connecting 
 to Wi-Fi\n	Installing and using apps\n	Troubleshooting common device 
 problems\n	Learning basic computer or tablet skills\n	Getting started with 
 browsers and the internet\n	Asking any tech question\n\n\nWhat to 
 Bring\n\n\n	Computer\n	Tablet\n	Tablet\n	Laptop\n	Any device you need help 
 with (and any relevant passwords\, if possible)\n\n\nWho Should 
 Attend\n\n\n	Anyone with questions about technology\n	People who want to 
 improve their tech skills\n	Those who want hands-on help or 
 troubleshooting\n\n\nFor more information\, please contact\n\nJason: 
 jchoward@dconc.gov\n\n
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Adult Computer Area\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jason Howard":MAILTO:jchoward@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Digital/Tech Literacy
