BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260509T180000Z
DTEND:20260509T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mallarmé Family Concert: The Woman Who Fell From the Sky and other stories
DESCRIPTION:Join Mallarmé as we present the New River Ensemble as they 
 tell an indigenous American story of the creation of the world and the 
 story of John Henry and automation in life today. There will be a tour the 
 zoo with music from Saint-Saëns’ Carnival of the Animals and a 
 re-imagining of songs for beginning musicians Book 1: The Klezmer Set and 
 our arrangements from Debussy’s Children’s Corner.\n\nFamily Concerts 
 are hour-long concerts appropriate for anyone 5 years and older and are 
 FREE! \n\nNew River Ensemble draws upon a wide array of influences to 
 present chamber music programs for general audiences and for kids and 
 families\, film scores\, and educational workshops that tug at the 
 boundaries that traditionally bind “chamber music ensembles.” NRE moves 
 smoothly from standard repertoire to modern composition\, from extended 
 techniques to improvisation. Their programs juxtapose pieces from different 
 time periods and genres\, challenging audiences to hear these pieces in a 
 new light. In addition to mining the clarinet and flute trio repertoire of 
 the past centuries\, NRE arranges and composes much of their own music. The 
 members of NRE are Martha Hyde (clarinet\, flute\, saxophone\, composer)\, 
 Lisa Liske (cello)\, and Brendan Cooney (piano\, plucked 
 strings).\n\nSponsored by Mark and Cindy Kuhn
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Music
UID:LibCal-14288-15210315
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15210315
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260509T180000Z
DTEND:20260509T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T000000Z
SUMMARY:Listen up Bull City! Jazz Listening Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Slide on in and catch the groove! Our Jazz Listening Series in 
 collaboration with the legendary North Carolina Central University Jazz 
 Studies Program is back!  We’re bringing the soul\, the swing\, the 
 stories\, and the shine of Black musical brilliance right into the historic 
 Stanford L. Warren Library.\n\nEach session is a fun\, 
 come‑as‑you‑are listening hangout where we spin classic cuts\, 
 uncover hidden gems\, and spotlight the Black innovators who shaped jazz 
 from the Carolinas to the world. With insight and vibes straight from 
 NCCU’s award‑winning faculty\, students\, and alumni\, and local area 
 jazz afficionados you’ll hear the music—and the culture—through the 
 ears of real jazz insiders.\n\nExpect laughter\, lively conversation\, and 
 plenty of “Wait\, who was THAT?” moments as we celebrate the rhythms\, 
 roots\, and rich traditions of African American jazz.\n\nPull up\, tap in\, 
 and let’s groove together. The music is fire\, the company is warm\, and 
 the culture is ours to celebrate.
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Full Room\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carter Cue":MAILTO:ccue@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16632426
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16632426
END:VEVENT
