BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260511T220000Z
DTEND:20260511T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Magic of Louis Sachar
DESCRIPTION:\n\nJoin us for a very special event as we welcome Louis 
 Sachar\, the #1 New York Times bestselling author of "Holes". From the 
 wacky hallways of "Wayside School" to the heartwarming humor of "There’s 
 a Boy in the Girls’ Bathroom"\, Sachar’s stories have defined childhood 
 for generations.\n\nNow\, he joins us to discuss his celebrated career and 
 his first venture into fiction for adults\,\n\n"The Magician of Tiger 
 Castle".\n\n\n\nLouis Sachar has been writing children’s books for over 
 thirty years. He is best known for his Newbery Medal and National Book 
 Award-winning novel Holes\, which was adapted into a 2003 film of the same 
 name. He is also the author of both the Sideways Stories From a Wayside 
 School and the Marvin Redpost series\, as well as many other critically 
 acclaimed novels. His most recent middle grade novel\, Fuzzy Mud\, is a 
 cautionary environmental  tale that features both mystery and 
 humor.\n\nSachar’s lectures are as imaginative and entertaining as his 
 works of fiction\, and he enjoys speaking to audiences of all ages on the 
 writing process and sharing the backstories of how his bestselling novels 
 came to be.\n\nSachar was born in New York and raised in California\, where 
 he attended college and law school. While working in an elementary school 
 during college\, he was inspired to begin writing books for children. His 
 middle grade novels often feature complex characters\, struggling through 
 captivating adventures and are beloved by children and educators alike. He 
 lives in Austin\, Texas with his family.\n\n\nThis event is brought to you 
 by Durham County library Humanities\n\n \n\nand Sponsored by Durham Library 
 Foundation\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWhere can I park when the Main Library parking lot 
 is full?\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the North 
 Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the 
 apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking is free in 
 the garage. Please bring your ticket to a service desk in the library for 
 validation.\n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Durham Library Foundation, Humanities, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16727347
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16727347
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260511T220000Z
DTEND:20260511T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T000000Z
SUMMARY:Using Data to Build Your Business
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\nHave a great business idea but need solid 
 data to back it up? Join us for a hands-on workshop where we’ll guide you 
 step-by-step through the library’s powerful business databases and 
 research tools. Learn how to find market trends\, analyze competitors\, and 
 gather data that supports your business plan. Perfect for entrepreneurs and 
 small business owners ready to make informed decisions. Whether you’re 
 launching a startup or growing an existing business\, this workshop will 
 give you the blueprint you need to succeed.\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-16080966
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16080966
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260511T223000Z
DTEND:20260511T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club -- A Study in Scarlet Women
DESCRIPTION:Join us virtually\, or in person\, this month to discuss A 
 Study in Scarlet Women.\n\nUSA Today bestselling author Sherry Thomas turns 
 the story of the renowned Sherlock Holmes upside down.\n\nWith her 
 inquisitive mind\, Charlotte Holmes has never felt comfortable with the 
 demureness expected of the fairer sex in upper-class society. But even she 
 never thought that she would become a social pariah\, an outcast fending 
 for herself on the mean streets of London.\n\nWhen the city is struck by a 
 trio of unexpected deaths and suspicion falls on her sister and her 
 father\, Charlotte is desperate to find the true culprits and clear the 
 family name. She'll have help from friends new and old\, but in the end\, 
 it will be up to Charlotte\, under the assumed name Sherlock Holmes\, to 
 challenge society's expectations and match wits against an unseen 
 mastermind.\n\nClick below for format availability:\n\nDurham 
 County\n\nOrange County\n\nWake County\n\nAdditionally\, there will be 
 physical copies available at the North Regional Information Desk while 
 supplies last.\n\nRegistration is required to receive the Zoom link to 
 attend the event.\n\nE-mail Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Dominique Diggs":MAILTO:fdiggs@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-15134858
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15134858
END:VEVENT
