BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260513T170000Z
DTEND:20260513T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: To the Lighthouse
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 To the Lighthouse by Virginia Woolf. The description for the book is 
 below:\n"To the Lighthouse is made up of three powerfully charged visions 
 into the life of the Ramsay family living in a summer house off the rocky 
 coast of Scotland. There's the serene and maternal Mrs. Ramsay\, the tragic 
 yet absurd Mr. Ramsay\, their eight children\, and assorted holiday guests. 
 With the lighthouse excursion postponed\, Woolf shows the small joys and 
 quiet tragedies of everyday life that seemingly could go on forever.\n\nBut 
 as time winds its way through their lives\, the Ramsays face\, alone and 
 together\, the greatest of human challenges and its greatest triumph--the 
 human capacity for change.\n\nA moving portrait in miniature of family 
 life\, To the Lighthouse also has profoundly universal implications\, 
 giving language to the silent space that separates people and the space 
 that they transgress to reach each other."\n\nWe look forward to seeing you 
 all soon!\n\n\nInterested in attending a future Daytime Book Club meeting? 
 Take a look at our reading list below:\n\nMay 2026: To the Lighthouse by 
 Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: The Night Watchman by Louise Erdrich\n\nJuly 
 2026: A Marriage at Sea by Sophie Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: My Friends by 
 Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 2026: Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte 
 McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on Mango Street by Sandra 
 Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil by John 
 Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What 
 We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: Song of Solomon by Toni 
 Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by 
 Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576121
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576121
END:VEVENT
