SUMMARY:Miniature Books and Bookcases!
DESCRIPTION:Love books and reading? Love your library? Love miniatures?  
 \n\nDrop in between 5:30-7 p.m. to craft miniature books and bookcases out 
 of recycled materials! Store your miniature books in a miniature 
 bookcase!\n\nCustomize your books and bookcases to reflect you!  
 \n\nSupplies like decorative paper\, miniature objects\, and stickers are 
 provided but please bring your own Altoids tin and anything else you would 
 like to use or add to your miniature books and bookcase! \n\nBookcases will 
 be made with reused Altoid tins with dimensions of 3.75inches long\, 2.375 
 inches wide\, and 0.75 inches deep.  \n\nThe program is appropriate for 
 adults and juveniles of all ages with an adult guardian present. Please 
 register everyone attending   \n\nDrop in between 5:30 p.m. through 7 p.m. 
 on May 13th for an open crafting session in the MakerLab located on the 
 first floor of the Durham County Main Library. Volunteers will be on hand 
 for assistance with the construction of the mini books and bookcases.  
 \n\nRegistration is required to ensure there are enough crafting supplies 
 available for participants. Please cancel your registration if you are 
 unable to attend so that those on the waitlist may attend.   \n\nQuestions? 
 Contact mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
