DTSTAMP:20260513T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through June. Register for the 
 weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or accommodation 
 needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or call 
 919-560-9940\n\n\nÚnase a un ambiente de apoyo para cursos de habilidades 
 digitales a su propio ritmo. Usaremos Northstar Digital Literacy\, un 
 recurso en línea gratuito que también está disponible en español para 
 todos los usuarios de la Biblioteca del Condado de Durham. Un miembro del 
 personal de la biblioteca estará presente para ayudarle a comenzar y 
 responder sus preguntas mientras cada participante avanza por los módulos 
 en línea de manera individual y a su propio ritmo. Northstar le permite 
 llevar un registro de su progreso y obtener insignias o certificados al 
 completar un curso. Estas clases son ideales para personas que ya cuentan 
 con habilidades básicas de teclado y mouse. Nuestro laboratorio de 
 computación tiene una cantidad limitada de laptops disponibles\, por lo 
 que se recomienda traer su propio laptop y audífonos.\n\nLos temas de 
 computación y habilidades digitales incluyen:\n\n\n	Conceptos básicos del 
 teclado del teléfono e inicio de sesión\n	Habilidades básicas de 
 computación\n	Conceptos básicos de Internet\n	Uso del correo 
 electrónico\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel y 
 PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Redes sociales\n	Alfabetización 
 informacional\n	Habilidades para la búsqueda de empleo\n	Su huella 
 digital\n	Cómo acceder a citas de telesalud\n	Conceptos básicos de 
 ciberseguridad\n\n\nEstas clases son autodirigidas y cada semana los 
 participantes elegirán qué lecciones desean completar por su cuenta. No 
 necesita haber asistido a la primera clase para participar en las 
 siguientes sesiones\, y no es necesario comprometerse a todas las clases 
 hasta junio. ¡Inscríbase en las semanas que mejor le funcionen!\n\nSi 
 tiene preguntas o necesita alguna adaptación\, comuníquese con Jimmy 
 McKinnell a jmckinnell@dconc.gov o llame al 919-560-9940.\n
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16677660
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16677660
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260513T220000Z
DTEND:20260513T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T000000Z
SUMMARY:Youth Justice and Disability Rights
DESCRIPTION:Join Disability Rights North Carolina at the Durham Main 
 Library for a critical conversation on youth justice and disability rights. 
 From July 2024 through August 2025\, staff at Disability Rights North 
 Carolina conducted nearly 400 in-person interviews with youth confined in 
 each of the then 14 operating Juvenile Detention Centers in the State. They 
 found that youth in NC's Juvenile Detention Centers receive dramatically 
 different treatment\, education services\, and other rehabilitative 
 opportunities depending on the facility in which they are detained - and 
 most of the facilities violate state policies regarding their operations\, 
 including the use of solitary confinement in some of the facilities\, 
 including Durham County Youth Home. \n\nThe event will highlight details of 
 the report\, especially as they related to the Durham County Youth Home\, 
 and a panel of advocates will follow\, sharing insights\, lived 
 experiences\, and strategies for change. Come learn\, connect\, and be part 
 of efforts to promote safer\, more just conditions for young people.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Durham, Law
UID:LibCal-14288-16563504
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16563504
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260513T220000Z
DTEND:20260513T234500Z
