SUMMARY:Read to Me Pet Partners
DESCRIPTION:Relax and read with a dog and other animals! This program 
 brings dogs and reluctant readers together for 15 minutes of companionship. 
 Handlers and their dogs provide quiet encouragement to children so that 
 they might develop a love of reading and improve communication skills. 
 \n\nPlease note that you may book one session per day\, and sessions are 15 
 minutes long. Available time slots are as follows: 10: 00a.m\, 10: 20a.m\, 
 and 10:40a.m. \n\nRegistration is required. Please call Molly at 
 919-560-0234 or email mschaefer@dconc.gov with your preferred time and your 
 contact information. \n\nEvent details: \n\n\n	Location: Durham County 
 North Regional Library\n	Date: Saturday\, May 16\, 2026 \n	Time: 10:00 a.m. 
 \n	Address: 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712 \n\n\n
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16462518
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16462518
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
DTEND:20260516T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T000000Z
SUMMARY:Nature Writing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Nature has inspired countless pieces of poetry and prose over 
 the course of time and space\; writing about nature puts us in intimate 
 touch with our own inner landscapes\, while filling us with awe and 
 reverence for our natural world. If you have ever been curious about nature 
 writing - what it is and how to get started - or if you already consider 
 yourself a nature writer and would like more experience\, guidance\, and 
 community\, this writing workshop is for you! We will walk through nature 
 visualizations/meditations\, explore writing prompts as a group\, share our 
 work and provide thoughts and reflections on each others' work\, and spend 
 time with some powerful selections from the vast canon of nature writing. 
 Open to all experience levels. Just bring yourselves\, a notebook\, and a 
 writing implement. Prior attendance is NOT required.\n\nChiara has been 
 writing for most of her life\, primarily poetry\; she has a degree in 
 English Literature from Syracuse University\, and a Masters of 
 Environmental Management from Duke University. Chiara has spent many years 
 as an environmental educator\, is Level 1 Ecotherapy certified\, and 
 completed a fellowship program with the Center for Education\, 
 Imagination\, & The Natural World entitled "The Inner Life of the Child in 
 Nature: Presence & Practice." Chiara has been published in Duke 
 University's Eno Magazine and in the North Carolina Bards 2021 Anthology. 
 As well\, she has put out a self-published poetry collection entitled "The 
 Taxonomy of Longing."\n\nThis session will take place in our 3rd floor 
 Conference Room\, 3214. \n\n
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Environmental, Humanities, Literacy, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16550678
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16550678
END:VEVENT
